"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JQCK4WZX1S0ANXP\",\"title\":\"Project Juniper — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"CANCELED\",\"DAC\",\"Project Juniper\",\"Clairity\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Project code\",\"E9MP\",\"PROTOCOL DETAILS\",\"Current protocol version\",\"Direct Air Capture v1.1\",\"Accreditation\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"E9MP\",\"approval\":null,\"protocol_current\":\"Direct Air Capture v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"25 May 2025\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"25 Apr 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://clairitytech.com\",\"t\":\"Clairity\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/direct-air-capture/1.1\",\"t\":\"Direct Air Capture v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JJXVJ35P1S0P0BS\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JJXVJ35P1S0P0BS/prj_1JQCK4WZX1S0ANXP/pjd_1JXMGCT2T1S09QJB/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JJXVJ35P1S0P0BS/prj_1JQCK4WZX1S0ANXP/pjd_1JSQ1JQEG1S0DEE1/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"CANCELED\\nDAC\\nProject Juniper\\nClairity\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nProject code\\nE9MP\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nDirect Air Capture v1.1\\nAccreditation\\nSummary\\n\\nProject Juniper is a direct air capture (DAC) and ex-situ mineralization project owned by Clairity and operated by Clairity. Project Juniper captures atmospheric CO2 using Clairity’s novel, low-cost, and scalable approach to DAC, storing CO2 permanently in carbonated materials using a closed, engineered ex-situ mineralization process. Project Juniper is carbon negative and water positive, generating water for water-stressed communities in the Southern Nevada region where the project is located. Project Juniper is fully electric and can be powered by clean energy from the local grid operator.\\n\\nJuniper\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nDirect Air Capture (DAC) encompasses technologies that remove carbon dioxide directly from the atmosphere using chemical or electrochemical processes. Typically, in DAC, carbon dioxide in the air binds to either a solid sorbent or a liquid solvent, which then undergoes a regeneration process to release the carbon. The captured carbon dioxide can then be permanently stored using a range of techniques, including deep underground in geological formations.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 24 May 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2025\\nSite visit\\n2026\\nProject canceled\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n25 May 2025\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n25 Apr 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"